  "limitations": [
    "Small local lab run; no confidence intervals or dedicated quiet host.",
    "UI fixture excludes real server/SDK latency, live profiler updates and emulator decode; narrow layout is desktop Chromium resized, not a physical phone.",
    "Two animation frames set a roughly 33ms floor on UI probes; these are not INP measurements.",
    "CPU percentages are relative to one core. Memory is sampled PSS/RSS, not a leak test or isolated allocation cost.",
    "Operational Android A/B uses ADB frame polling without SDK and SDK frame delivery with SDK, so it is not an isolated pure-SDK microbenchmark.",
    "No data writes, heavy joins, large real databases, physical-device performance, long-running memory soak or frame-source-matched A/B were tested.",
    "Android PSS probes used meminfo -s without --local and can induce GC; these are post-dump snapshots, not steady-state memory or allocations."
  ]
